.TH DOT-MAN 1 "September 2026" "dot-man 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dot-man \- git-powered dotfile manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dot-man
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
dot-man tracks your dotfiles in git. Each branch is a complete
configuration (work, personal, minimal, server) — switch between them
and dot-man saves the current state, deploys the target files, and runs
your hooks.
.PP
Everyday workflow:
.BR init ,
.BR add ,
.BR status ,
.BR navigate .
Run
.B "dot-man help-all"
for the full command list.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B "init [--no-wizard]"
Initialize a new dot-man repository (interactive wizard by default).
.TP
.B "add <path>"
Track a file or directory.
.TP
.B status
Show tracked files and pending changes.
.TP
.B "navigate <branch>"
Save current changes and switch to another configuration branch, tag,
or commit. Alias:
.BR nav .
.TP
.B "deploy <branch>"
One-way deployment of a branch configuration.
.TP
.B doctor
Run diagnostics and health checks.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --help
Show the happy-path commands.
.TP
.BR --version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BR "-v, --verbose"
Show detailed output on console.
.TP
.BR --debug
Enable debug logging to file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/dot-man/
Configuration directory (repository, global config, hooks).
.TP
.I ~/.config/dot-man/repo/dot-man.toml
Section definitions: which paths to track and their hooks.
.TP
.I <repo>/hooks/
Versioned hook scripts, referenced as
.BR "file:<script>" .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Full reference: https://beshoyehab.github.io/dot-man/
.SH AUTHOR
dot-man contributors.
